<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sistan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sakastan, Seistan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sistan is a region in the basin of the Helmand river and Lake Hamun, divided today between south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>. The ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drangiana">Drangiana</a>, it took the name Sakastan, 'land of the Saka', after Saka nomads settled there in the late second century BCE. Irrigated farming made it prosperous for centuries, and in Persian epic it is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the hero <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rostam">Rostam</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sistan.jpg" alt="Sistan" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dolphinphoto5d · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Asiyab_badi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
